<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43906" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐήλᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαύνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy to drive</i> or <i>ride over</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεδία</span>
			<i>fit for cavalry operations</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.4.16
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>HG</u>
				5.4.54
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τῆς ἀρετῆς [ὁδὸς] τὰ πρῶτα οὐκ
					εὐήλατά κως παρέχειν δοκέει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eus.Mynd.
					63
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>well-ground</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλφι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antim.
					64
				</span></i>
			; <i>well-hammered</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euph.
					51.10
				</span></i>
			.</div>
